{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** There are `numCourses` courses, numbered `0` to `numCourses - 1`. Each pair `[course, pre]` in `prerequisites` means you must take `pre` before `course`. Return `true` if you can finish every course."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/f2ff9a06-b98b-4178-b229-2d764ad06e19.svg",
      "alt": "Left: four courses with arrows from each prerequisite to the course it unlocks: 0 to 1, 0 to 2, 1 to 3 and 2 to 3. They can be taken in the order 0, 1, 2, 3. Right: three courses whose arrows form a loop, 0 to 1 to 2 and back to 0, in red: none of them can ever be taken first.",
      "width": 647,
      "height": 383,
